{"text": "3.\n\nOPEGA Review Request Form\n\nOffice of Program Evaluation and Government Accountability\n\nPlease complete this form with information that is as specific as possible. Use additional\npages as necessary. If you wish to submit your request in a letter please include as many\nof the details asked for on this form as possible. You may be contacted by OPEGA and\nasked for additional information. If you have questions about the form or the request\nprocess, please contact OPEGA at 207-287-1901.\n\n\u2018What is the name of the department, program or function that you want OPEGA to review/audit?\n\n|, Rep. Jeffrey Timberlake, would like to formally request that OPEGA review/aualt the Fund for Healthy Maine. | know a\nmajority of the money used to fund this program comes from the tobacco settlement, but | would ike to knaw how much\ntaxpayer money is included as wel.\n\n\u2018What concerns have led you to request an OPEGA review?\n\n\u2018The Fund for Healthy Maine receives a significant amount of taxpayer dollars annually. AS a member of the appropriations\n\u2018committee, Ihave sought answers to my questions, but have been unsuccessful. | have not been provided with a precise\nbreakdown of how the money is spent. Maine taxpayers deserve to know how thelr money is being used to ensure that itis\nbeing priortized propery,\n\nWhat specific questions would you like an OPEGA review to answer?\n1. How much money is given to the Fund for Healthy Maine annually?\nDoes appropriated money go into a separate bank account?\nHow much money is spent on administrative costs annually?\nOf the allocated money, how much Is spent on projects/programs for Mainers?\nWhat happens to the money that is unspent?\nHow much money is allocated for Planned Parenthood?\nDoes the Fund for Healthy Maine know where/how Planned Parenthood spends those funds?\n\nDoes the Legislature supplement the Fund For Healthy Maine tobacco settlement money> If so, is\nthere a history of the allocations?\n\n9. Is there a list of recipients who have received Fund for Healthy Maine money? How much of those funds\nwere not spent and were returned to the Fund for Healthy Maine?\n\n2@rASBEYN\n\n\u2018What potential beneficial outcomes do you expect may come from OPEGA performing this review?\n\n| believe that by conducting this review, money given to the Fund for Healthy Maine by the Legislature willbe better\nprioritized. It's my hope that this review will help the Fund for Healthy Maine better serve the Maine taxpayer.",
